\begin_layout Enumerate
Determine how 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{H}$
\end_inset

 transforms the classical states 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{0}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{1}$
\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

#+html:
 <details><summary>Show/hide solution...</summary>Start with 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{0}$
\end_inset

:
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align}
\mathbf{H}\ket{0} & =\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\mathbf{X}+\mathbf{Z}\right)\right)\ket{0}\nonumber \\
 & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\mathbf{X}\ket{0}+\mathbf{Z}\ket{0}\right)\nonumber \\
 & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\ket{1}+\ket{0}\right)=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\ket{0}+\ket{1}\right)\equiv\ket{+}\label{eq:Hket0}
\end{align}

\end_inset

Here,
 we have used Equation 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:defHadamard"

\end_inset

 to expand 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{H}$
\end_inset

,
 and we have used the action of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{H}$
\end_inset

 on 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{0}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{1}$
\end_inset

 from the previous exercise,
 see 
\begin_inset Note Note
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
Equations 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:Zket0"

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:Zket1"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset


\end_layout

\end_inset

.
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align}
\mathbf{H}\ket{1} & =\left(\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\mathbf{X}+\mathbf{Z}\right)\right)\ket{1}\nonumber \\
 & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\mathbf{X}\ket{1}+\mathbf{Z}\ket{1}\right)\nonumber \\
 & =\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\ket{0}-\ket{1}\right)\equiv\ket{-}\label{eq:Hket1}
\end{align}

\end_inset

Here,
 we have defined the kets 
\begin_inset Formula $\ket{\pm}$
\end_inset

 as a compact shorthand for writing 
\begin_inset Formula $\left(1/\sqrt{2}\right)\left(\ket{0}\pm\ket{1}\right)$
\end_inset

.
 We can then write these states as column vectors:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\ket{\pm}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left(\ket{0}\pm\ket{1}\right)\qquad\leftrightarrow\qquad\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left[\begin{array}{c}
1\\
\pm1
\end{array}\right]
\]

\end_inset

#+html:
 </details>
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Find the matrix representation of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{H}$
\end_inset

 in the computational basis.
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

#+html:
 <details><summary>Show/hide solution...</summary>We can construct the matrix representation of 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbf{H}$
\end_inset

 in a column-wise manner:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
\mathbf{H}=\left[\begin{array}{cc}
\mathbf{H}\ket{0} & \mathbf{H}\ket{1}\end{array}\right]=\frac{1}{\sqrt{2}}\left[\begin{array}{cc}
1 & 1\\
1 & -1
\end{array}\right]
\]

\end_inset

Alternately,
 we could use Equations 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:sigmax"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "eq:sigma_y_z_more_common"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"
nolink "false"

\end_inset

.
